#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "1. Introduction {#1-introduction}"
msgstr "1. Pendahuluan {#1-introduction}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This lesson explores modern quantum computing hardware.\n"
msgstr "Pelajaran ini mengeksplorasi perangkat keras komputasi kuantum modern.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We will start by verifying some versions and importing some relevant packages.\n"
msgstr "Kita akan mulai dengan memverifikasi beberapa versi dan mengimpor beberapa paket yang relevan.\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "2. Backend and Target {#2-backend-and-target}"
msgstr "2. Backend dan Target {#2-backend-and-target}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Qiskit provides an API to obtain the information, both static and dynamic, about a quantum device. We use a Backend instance to interface with a device, which includes a Target instance, an abstract machine model that summarizes the pertinent features such as its instruction set architecture (ISA) and any properties or constraints associated with it.\n"
"Let us use these backend instances to get some of the information you see on the [Compute resources](https://quantum.cloud.ibm.com/computers) page\n"
"on IBM Quantum&reg; Platform.   First, we create a backend instance for a device of interest.  In the following, we pick \"ibm_kyoto\" , \"ibm_kawasaki\" or the least busy Eagle machine. Your access to QPUs might differ; update the backend name accordingly.\n"
msgstr ""
"Qiskit menyediakan API untuk mendapatkan informasi, baik statis maupun dinamis, tentang perangkat kuantum. Kita menggunakan instance Backend untuk berinteraksi dengan perangkat, yang mencakup instance Target, sebuah model mesin abstrak yang merangkum fitur-fitur penting seperti instruction set architecture (ISA)-nya dan properti atau batasan apa pun yang terkait dengannya.\n"
"Mari gunakan instance Backend ini untuk mendapatkan beberapa informasi yang kamu lihat di halaman [Compute resources](https://quantum.cloud.ibm.com/computers)\n"
"di IBM Quantum&reg; Platform. Pertama, kita buat instance Backend untuk perangkat yang diinginkan. Berikut, kita memilih \"ibm_kyoto\", \"ibm_kawasaki\" atau mesin Eagle yang paling tidak sibuk. Aksesmu ke QPU mungkin berbeda; perbarui nama Backend sesuai kebutuhan.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We start with some basic (static) information about the device.\n"
msgstr "Kita mulai dengan beberapa informasi dasar (statis) tentang perangkat.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "2.1 Exercise {#21-exercise}"
msgstr "2.1 Latihan {#21-exercise}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Try to get the basic information about a Heron device, \"ibm_strasbourg\". Try this on your own, but code has been added below for you to check yourself.\n"
msgstr "Coba dapatkan informasi dasar tentang perangkat Heron, \"ibm_strasbourg\". Coba sendiri dulu, tetapi kode telah ditambahkan di bawah agar kamu bisa memeriksanya sendiri.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "2.2 Coupling map {#22-coupling-map}"
msgstr "2.2 Coupling map {#22-coupling-map}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We now draw the coupling map of the device. As you can see, nodes are qubits which are numbered. Edges indicate pairs to which you can directly apply the 2-qubit entangling gate.  The topology is called a \"heavy-hex lattice\".\n"
msgstr "Kita sekarang menggambar coupling map dari perangkat. Seperti yang bisa kamu lihat, node adalah qubit yang dinomori. Edge menunjukkan pasangan yang padanya kamu bisa langsung menerapkan Gate entangling 2-Qubit. Topologinya disebut \"kisi heavy-hex\".\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/utility-scale-quantum-computing/hardware/extracted-outputs/51b87458-a5e8-4e77-a34d-39fe425a5f01-0.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Output dari sel kode sebelumnya](/learning/images/courses/utility-scale-quantum-computing/hardware/extracted-outputs/51b87458-a5e8-4e77-a34d-39fe425a5f01-0.avif)\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "3. Qubit properties {#3-qubit-properties}"
msgstr "3. Properti qubit {#3-qubit-properties}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The Eagle device has 127 qubits.   Let us obtain the properties of some of them.\n"
msgstr "Perangkat Eagle memiliki 127 qubit. Mari dapatkan properti beberapa di antaranya.\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Let us calculate the median of T1 times of the qubits.   Compare the result to the one shown for the device on [IBM Quantum Platform](https://quantum.cloud.ibm.com/).\n"
msgstr "Mari hitung median waktu T1 dari qubit. Bandingkan hasilnya dengan yang ditampilkan untuk perangkat di [IBM Quantum Platform.](https://quantum.cloud.ibm.com/)\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "3.1 Exercise {#31-exercise}"
msgstr "3.1 Latihan {#31-exercise}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Pease calculate the median of T2 times of the qubits. Try this on your own, but code has been added below for you to check yourself.\n"
msgstr "Silakan hitung median waktu T2 dari qubit. Coba sendiri dulu, tetapi kode telah ditambahkan di bawah agar kamu bisa memeriksanya sendiri.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "3.2 Gate and readout errors {#32-gate-and-readout-errors}"
msgstr "3.2 Error Gate dan readout {#32-gate-and-readout-errors}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We now turn to gate errors. To begin with, we study the data structure of the target instance. It is a dictionary whose keys are operation names.\n"
msgstr "Kita sekarang beralih ke error Gate. Pertama, kita pelajari struktur data dari instance target. Ini adalah kamus yang kuncinya adalah nama operasi.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Its values are also dictionaries.  Let us look at some of the items of the value (dictionary) for the 'sx' operation.\n"
msgstr "Nilainya juga berupa kamus. Mari lihat beberapa item dari nilai (kamus) untuk operasi 'sx'.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Let us do the same for the 'ecr' and 'measure' operations.\n"
msgstr "Mari lakukan hal yang sama untuk operasi 'ecr' dan 'measure'.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "As you can see, the errors of readout tend to be larger than those of the 2-qubit operation, which in turn tend to be larger than the 1-qubit operation.\n"
msgstr "Seperti yang bisa kamu lihat, error readout cenderung lebih besar dari operasi 2-Qubit, yang pada gilirannya cenderung lebih besar dari operasi 1-Qubit.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, fuzzy, no-wrap
#| msgid "Having understood the data structures, we are ready to calculate the median errors for the 'sx' and the 'ecr' gates. Again, compare the results with the ones shown for the device on the [IBM Quantum Platform.](https://quantum.cloud.ibm.com/)\n"
msgid "Having understood the data structures, we are ready to calculate the median errors for the 'sx' and the 'ecr' gates. Again, compare the results with the ones shown for the device on [IBM Quantum Platform](https://quantum.cloud.ibm.com/).\n"
msgstr "Setelah memahami struktur data, kita siap untuk menghitung error median untuk Gate 'sx' dan 'ecr'. Sekali lagi, bandingkan hasilnya dengan yang ditampilkan untuk perangkat di [IBM Quantum Platform.](https://quantum.cloud.ibm.com/)\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "4. Appendix {#4-appendix}"
msgstr "4. Lampiran {#4-appendix}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "A popular feature of Qiskit is its visualization capability. It includes circuit visualizers, state and distribution visualizers, and target visualizer.   You already used the first two in the previous jupyter notebooks.   Let us use some capabilities of the target visualizer.\n"
msgstr "Fitur populer dari Qiskit adalah kemampuan visualisasinya. Ini mencakup visualisasi Circuit, state dan distribusi, serta visualisasi target. Kamu sudah menggunakan dua yang pertama di notebook jupyter sebelumnya. Mari gunakan beberapa kemampuan dari visualisasi target.\n"

